'''Iktotchi''' were a horned [[Sentience|sentient]] [[species]] from the [[moon]] [[Iktotch]]. [[Jedi Master]] [[Saesee Tiin]], a member of the [[Jedi High Council]] prior to and during the [[Clone Wars]], was an Iktotchi.

==Biology and appearance==
[[File:SaeseeTiin-AA.png|thumb|left|150px|The Iktotchi Jedi Master Saesee Tiin]]
The Iktotchi were a [[species]] of [[near-human]]s<ref name="Catalyst" /> distinguished by the two large, curved horns protruding downwards from their heads. They had a skin-tone often varying from peach to brown,<ref name="Databank" /> battering-ram foreheads with hardened, dense skin, and big, fleshy hands.<ref name="Catalyst" /> Their blood was colored red.<ref name="Identity Crisis">{{TBB|Identity Crisis}}</ref> Their natural habitat was rocky.<ref name="VE" />

==Iktotchi in the galaxy==
[[Saesee Tiin]] was an imposing Iktotchi who served as a [[Jedi Master]] and member of the [[Jedi High Council]] in the last [[Standard decade|decades]] of the [[Galactic Republic]] and most notably the [[Clone Wars]], during which, he died alongside [[Kit Fisto|three]] [[Agen Kolar|other]] [[Mace Windu|Jedi]] in an attempt to arrest Supreme Chancellor Palpatine.<ref name="Saesee Tiin">{{Databank|saesee-tiin|Saesee Tiin}}</ref>

[[Dagio Belcoze]] operated as a computer engineer with [[Doctor]] [[Gubacher]] during the period of [[Galen Walton Erso]]'s work with [[Project Celestial Power]]. Belcoze designed enhanced [[Overseer droid (Death Star)|overseer droids]], and entered into a drunken disagreement with Erso during a [[Republic Futures Program]] reunion at [[500 Republica]].<ref name="Catalyst" />

[[File:FerrenBarr-2017DarthVader16.png|thumb|200px|Ferren Bar, the Iktotchi Jedi Padawan who survived Order 66]][[Ferren Barr]] was a [[Jedi]] [[Padawan]] who survived [[Order 66]] and became an [[advisor]] to [[Mon Calamari]] [[King of Mon Cala|King]] [[Lee-Char]]. His notable feats include uncovering the details of the [[Great Jedi Purge]] and the truth of the Clone Wars, along with activating Order 66 on [[Purge Trooper]]s to use them on the [[Inquisitorius|Inquisitors]] who were after him. He was ultimately killed by [[Anakin Skywalker|Darth Vader]], but died knowing he played his part to assist the downfall of the [[Galactic Empire]] and the [[Sith]].<ref name="Dark Lord 14">[[Darth Vader (2017) 14|''Darth Vader'' (2017) 14]]</ref> Around the same time, a young Iktotchi named [[Eva]] was utilized by [[Doctor]] [[Royce Hemlock]] as a test subject for [[Project Necromancer]] at the secret Imperial [[Tantiss Base|research facility]] on [[Wayland]].<ref name="Identity Crisis" />

[[Talvee Chawin]] was a [[crime lord]] on [[Coruscant]]'s [[Level 1313]] around the time of the [[Battle of Endor]], and was known by his nickname of the Thorn&mdash;referring to his one remaining horn which curved under his chin with the appearance of a barbed, poisonous thorn.<ref name="Aftermath">[[Aftermath (novel)|''Aftermath'']]</ref>

[[Ax Tagrin]] was a [[bounty hunter]] active during the [[First Order-Resistance War]] who hunted and captured [[Resistance]] [[Spy|spies]] for the [[First Order]].<ref name="The Missing Agent">{{Resistance|The Missing Agent}}</ref>

